Z||000000||gusto||08-31-2001||02:44 AM||||Like I said in my last post, I just bought a '85 SE with minor problems. I hope someone can help with this new one. My brother checked my fuses, and only one was blown, but as soon as he replaced it one head light went down, and it will not come up. The other head light won't move. Any one have any idea why, and how easy/exspensive it is to fix?                                                                                                                           -thanks||||reg||9
Z||000001||StuGood||08-31-2001||04:42 PM||||I'm guessing that the fuse you replaced was the taillight fuse - the signal to tell the headlights to run down is powered by that fuse.  <P>You might want to check out the Michigan Fiero Club's web page.  They have a pretty good article on how to rebuild the headlight motors.  It takes more time than money.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||gusto||09-01-2001||06:08 PM||||thanks for the advice. looks like my motor is fine though, the light wont come up cause the fuse blew as soon as i put it in, any ideas why it blows the fuse so fast?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mickey_Moose||09-02-2001||11:28 AM||||1) wrong size fuse<P>2) shorted wiring - check wiring for bare spots that are rubbing on the frame<P>3) motor no good - drawing too much current, blows the fuse<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||1
